# WinkUI UI consistency — same action, same control

When a control does the **exact same job** (copy, theme toggle, search clear, …), reuse the **existing shared component**. Do not invent a one-off unless the user explicitly asks for a different look or behavior.

## Copy (canonical)

- Use `CopyButton` from `@/components/docs` everywhere copy-to-clipboard is needed.
- Code samples: wrap with `ComponentSource` from `@/components/docs` (includes the copy icon). Do **not** hand-roll a second copy icon or a labeled “Copy” text button for the same action.
- Code theme: shiki `dark-plus` (VS Code Dark+) + `--code-*` chrome. Do not invent per-page zinc/primary code colors.
- Appearance: simple ghost **icon-only** button — Lucide `CopyIcon` idle, `CheckIcon` after success. No toast required unless asked.

```tsx
// ✅
import { CopyButton, ComponentSource } from "@/components/docs"

<ComponentSource title="button.tsx" code={source} />
<CopyButton value={cliCommand} />

// ❌ Duplicate / divergent copy UIs
<button onClick={() => navigator.clipboard.writeText(code)}>Copy</button>
```

## General rule

| Situation | Do |
|---|---|
| Same action already has a shared control | Import and reuse it |
| New repeated action (2+ places) | Extract one shared component first |
| User asks for a different style for one spot | Only then diverge — and say so in the PR |

Applies to docs chrome (`app/`, `components/`). Do not change shipped `registry/` primitives for this rule unless the action lives there too.
